{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:7c0376ae0ea9eee1","name":"Encumbrance","source":{"id":"source:reference-7c0376ae0ea9eee1","title":"Encumbrance","revision":18325,"timestamp":"2024-08-25T19:57:48Z","sha256":"373d26c8acb1ae4722091c03423f4677849236b91ba1fa20aca5ec0a45c9caa0","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=18325","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Encumbrance&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-7c0376ae0ea9eee1","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Core Rulebook"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Core_Rulebook"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Encumbrance rules determine how much Equipment slows you down. Encumbrance comes in two parts: Encumbrance by Armor, and Encumbrance by Weight.\n"]},"\n\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Encumbrance by Armor"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Your armor defines your maximum ",{"tag":"a","children":["Dexterity"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Dexterity"}," bonus to ",{"tag":"a","children":["Reflex Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Reflex_Defense"},", your ",{"tag":"a","children":["Armor Check Penalty"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Armor_Check_Penalty"},", your ",{"tag":"a","children":["Speed"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Speed","referenceId":"reference:c372fee9b4566b85"},", and how fast you move when you ",{"tag":"a","children":["Run"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Run","referenceId":"reference:00d60e31a4e6b834"},". Unless your character is weak or carrying a lot of gear, that's all you need to know. The extra gear your character carries, such as weapons and ",{"tag":"a","children":["Medpacs"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Medpacs"},", won't slow your character any more than your Armor already does. If your character is carrying a really Heavy Load, however, then you'll need to calculate Encumbrance by Weight.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Encumbrance by Weight"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["If you want to determine whether your character's gear is heavy enough to slow them down (more than any ",{"tag":"a","children":["Armor"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Armor"}," already does), add up the weight of all the armor, weapons, and gear the character is carrying. If the total equals or exceeds the square of one-half your character's ",{"tag":"a","children":["Strength"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Strength"}," score, they are carrying a Heavy Load. For example, a character with ",{"tag":"a","children":["Strength"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Strength"}," 12 is carrying a Heavy Load if the total weight of their Armor and gear is 36 kg ((0.5 x 12)",{"tag":"sup","children":["2"]},") or more.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["When carrying a Heavy Load, a character takes a -10 penalty on checks made using the following ",{"tag":"a","children":["Skills"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Skills","referenceId":"reference:66d0f523a379b2de"},":\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"ul","children":[{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Acrobatics"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Acrobatics","referenceId":"reference:0d0b7eee2953750e"}]},"\n",{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Climb"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Climb","referenceId":"reference:98ca5f27d9642dc7"}]},"\n",{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Endurance"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Endurance","referenceId":"reference:98c8abf84e23ff3f"}]},"\n",{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Initiative"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Initiative","referenceId":"reference:3e687de48a6ad4e5"}]},"\n",{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Jump"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Jump","referenceId":"reference:9ee0ca3e24d60ea0"}]},"\n",{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Stealth"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Stealth","referenceId":"reference:526a40a447ddd7aa"}]},"\n",{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Swim"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Swim","referenceId":"reference:dd4fa375c70c4e42"}]}]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["A Heavy Load also reduces the character's ",{"tag":"a","children":["Speed"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Speed","referenceId":"reference:c372fee9b4566b85"}," to three-quarters normal (rounded down). A character can move up to three times their ",{"tag":"a","children":["Speed"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Speed","referenceId":"reference:c372fee9b4566b85"}," when ",{"tag":"a","children":["Running"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Running"}," with a Heavy Load (instead of four times).\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Carrying Capacity"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["The amount of Weight that you can lift (in kilograms) is based on your ",{"tag":"a","children":["Strength"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Strength"}," score, and determined by the following formula: (",{"tag":"a","children":["Strength"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Strength"}," score)",{"tag":"sup","children":["2"]}," x 0.5. For example, a character with a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Strength"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Strength"}," 15 can lift 112.5 kg ((15)",{"tag":"sup","children":["2"]},"x0.5). A character can strain to lift an amount of weight (in kilograms) equal to their ",{"tag":"a","children":["Strength"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Strength"}," score squared, but they can only stagger around with it. While overloaded in this way, a character loses any ",{"tag":"a","children":["Dexterity"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Dexterity"}," bonus to ",{"tag":"a","children":["Reflex Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Reflex_Defense"}," and can only move 1 square per round (as a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Full-Round Action"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Full-Round_Action"},").\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["A dragged object has less effective weight depending on the resistance of the surface as noted in the below table:\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"table","children":["\n",{"tag":"tbody","children":[{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"th","children":["SURFACE\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["MULTIPLIER\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Rough\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["1\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Normal\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["1/2\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Smooth/Wheeled\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["1/5\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Frictionless\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["1/10\n"]}]}]}]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Bigger or Smaller Creatures"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Larger creatures can carry more weight depending on their size category, just as small creatures can carry less depending on their size. Below is a table with the size of a character and their carry capacity multipliers:\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"table","children":["\n",{"tag":"tbody","children":[{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"th","children":["SIZE\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["MULTIPLIER\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["\n"],"rowspan":6},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["SIZE\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["MULTIPLIER\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Fine\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["x0.01\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Large\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["x2\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Diminutive\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["x0.25\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Huge\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["x5\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Tiny\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["x0.5\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Gargantuan\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["x10\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Small\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["x0.75\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Colossal\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["x20\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Medium\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["x1\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["\n"],"colspan":2}]}]}]},"\n","\n","\n","\n\n","\n\n","\n"]}}
